The comment `@@@ If a non-null value is returned, the key was present in the map before the removal.` indicates a condition on the return value: if the method returns a non-null value, then the key must have been present in the map before the operation.

To express this in an assert statement:
- We use `\result` to refer to the return value.
- We use `\old(this.containsKey(key))` to check whether the key was present before the method call.
- The implication is: if `\result != null`, then the key was present before (i.e., `\old(this.containsKey(key))` is true).

Thus, the correct assertion is:

<code>assert \result != null => \old(this.containsKey(key));</code>
